WEBVTT

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:04.440
I've come to deliver your oxygen!

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.400
CELL

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.400
Right. Thanks for all your hard work!

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.860
If you could stamp this receipt here, please...

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.450
RECEIVED

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.450
Thank you very much!

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.200
I'm wiped. I think I'll take a break.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.130
Someone's working his tail off.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.090
All right.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.630
I guess I'll make some energy.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:38.550
Whoa!

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.930
A-Are you all right?

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.650
S-Somebody help me!

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.400
Whoa!

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.690
- It's all your fault!
- Huh?

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.400
It's because of that oxygen you delivered!

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.800
EPISODE 7:
CAFFEINE, TEMPTATION, AND JEALOUSY

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:34.800
Did you hear?

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.760
There was another accident!

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:40.720
Yeah, you mean the kind
where oxygen turns into ROS, right?

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.180
<i>Reactive Oxygen Species (ROS).</i>

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:48.230
<i>A generic term for oxygen that's been altered
into a highly reactive chemical compound.</i>

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:52.270
<i>Highly oxidative,
they can cause cellular aging.</i>

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.190
Scary, huh?

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:57.940
We're not getting enough nutrients as it is.
We can't go on like this.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:00.240
Hey! You there!

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:05.200
I saw you! It was you who brought the oxygen
to the cell who had that accident, right?

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.410
Uh, y-yes.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:11.370
So, that was on you, right?
Well, screw you! Get your act together!

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:16.630
That's right! It turned into ROS
because of your lousy handling, am I right?

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.840
So, what are you going to do
to make it right?

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.220
Well...

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.090
I think you have the wrong idea.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.010
Hey man...

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:27.600
What we deliver is oxygen,
no question about it.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.480
I'm told that when oxygen turns into ROS...

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.980
it's almost always
because of the body's internal environment.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:37.650
<i>Risk factors for increased production of ROS
include an inadequate supply of nutrients...</i>

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.610
<i>such as Vitamin E,
due to aging or improper diet,</i>

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:44.450
<i>smoking and ultraviolet exposure.</i>

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:48.410
I get that you're all pretty worried,
but instead of pointing fingers...

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:52.120
why don't we all work together
for the sake of this world?

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.460
Oh, never mind. Let's go.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.920
Hey, I owe you one.
You really know your stuff, huh?

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:03.260
Well, this is the world we work in.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:08.510
But who knew that the oxygen we deliver
could end up hurting the cells?

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.980
Kind of hard to swallow, huh?

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:15.600
Oh hey, we've got
some place to be, remember?

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:19.070
Yeah, the awards ceremony
for rookie Red Blood Cells, was it?

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.240
What a drag!

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:22.950
You said it!

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.030
And now, it gives me pleasure to announce...

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:30.450
the winner of this term's Top Rookie Award,
for delivering the most oxygen...

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.460
AA2153, please join me on stage!

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.080
What, me?

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:41.010
Hey, isn't that your buddy? Wow!

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:42.670
Yeah, uh...

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.470
You're always hanging out with him, right?

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:46.970
So, does that mean you're a hotshot, too?

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:48.600
No, not me.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.890
<i>Hey! This is looking really bad!</i>

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.270
<i>That's it! You're on your own now!</i>

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.730
Right. I'm always...

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.400
<i>Let's get out of here!</i>

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:03.070
<i>I'm not running.</i>

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.740
<i>I can't allow myself to run away!</i>

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.330
<i>Even if I'm right next to him,
all I ever do is try to run away.</i>

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.710
<i>Look how far he's left me behind.</i>

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.250
Congratulations!

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:22.960
Please keep up the good work
as the pride of your class!

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.170
Yes, sir!

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:29.850
And as for the disappointing few
among you who missed their quotas,

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:33.890
now that you're Red Blood Cells,
delivering oxygen is all that matters.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:37.900
Follow this young man's example
and deliver oxygen to the best of your ability.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:50.780
Pretty impressive, that buddy of yours.
Top Rookie Award, huh?

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.740
So, how did you do?

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.370
Nothing to write home about.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:57.210
They should just do away
with ceremonies like this, huh?

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.330
They had them back in our day, too.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.550
It's probably just to let the higher-ups
pat themselves on the back!

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:05.840
The guys who get the awards
might get a kick out of it,

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:10.640
but for losers like us who miss quotas,
it's hell, am I right?

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.810
We know just how you feel.

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:19.400
It's the same for us. We work our tails off,
and our efforts go unacknowledged.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.310
So unfulfilling, huh?

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.020
- Want to come with us?
- Huh?

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.860
You know, somewhere
that'll give us a boost...

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:29.240
Somewhere that'll give us a boost?

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.280
You'll see when you get there.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.240
I...

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.330
I think I'll pass.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:38.580
Jeez, he's no fun.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.540
Well, he'll join us one of these days.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:45.000
That kid is one of us.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:47.970
Good work.

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:49.720
Uh, yeah.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:50.930
Where are you headed now?

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:52.930
The Sebaceous Gland in a scalp pore.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.220
Same here.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:55.430
Is that right?

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:00.600
Look, you don't have to slow down
for my sake, okay?

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.900
Since you're the Top Rookie and all.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:06.110
Hey, come on!
That was just totally random.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:09.070
Just be happy about it
because it's a great feat!

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:11.280
Huh? Yeah. Sorry.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.240
Oh no. No need to apologize or anything.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:21.500
We haven't been here
since the spot balding incident, huh?

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.960
PORES
HAIR ROOT

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:24.250
I wonder how the Hair Matrix Cells are doing.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:26.920
Huh?

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:29.880
There's no hair!

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:33.760
Either the hair roots are closed
or the hair's all thin.

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:36.850
And the Hair Matrix Cells
don't seem to have much energy.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.730
Hair Matrix Cell...
Long time no see.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:47.820
Oh, it's you. Thanks again for helping us
during the spot balding incident.

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:49.900
Hasn't there been
any hair growth since then?

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:54.870
Yeah, well, there's actually been more hair loss
thanks to poor circulation from stress.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.530
Oh, is that right?

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:58.830
Um, how do I get to the Sebaceous Gland?

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.790
Right, it's right above us.
You can ride up on that.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:11.260
It's supposed to be
at the top of these stairs.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:15.590
What, higher?
And we have to take the stairs?

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.850
What a workout,
getting up these stairs.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.820
I'll carry some of those cylinders in your box.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:29.860
It's okay.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:32.190
Don't worry. I can handle it.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.290
I said it's okay. I mean it.

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:35.320
You don't have to overdo it.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.280
Which part of "It's okay" don't you get?

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:40.540
Fine.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:55.930
Hey, what's up with that?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:56.890
That's...

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.350
ROS!

00:08:58.600 --> 00:08:59.430
What?

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:07.100
<i>Reactive Oxygen Species (ROS) attacks
the Red Blood Cells' membranes,</i>

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:10.150
<i>robbing them of their ability
to transport oxygen.</i>

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:11.280
Let's get out of here!

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:21.450
It looks like we're safe now!

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:24.290
This sucks! What the heck is going on?

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:27.250
SEBACEOUS GLAND

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:25.870
This way.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:27.250
Okay.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:31.960
Whoa, it's all oily in here!
What a filthy room!

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.170
My apologies.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:38.140
Oh hey, so you're here!
Sorry I said it was filthy.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:39.970
Please don't give it another thought.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:41.720
After all, it's true.

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.890
<i>Sebaceous Gland Cell.</i>

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:49.690
<i>Divides repeatedly inside the Sebaceous Gland
by the Pore, storing sebum.</i>

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.650
We've come to deliver your oxygen.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.780
I hate to trouble you,
but if you could kindly set one down there

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.780
and attach the other one outside...

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:01.780
As the Sebaceous Gland is ready to burst,
I can't move a muscle.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:02.620
Sure!

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:08.750
Is that all right?

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.960
Yes, I really appreciate it.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:14.340
Getting a delivery of fresh oxygen
on my last day!

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:15.970
What do you mean, your last day?

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:20.590
You see, I'm retiring today.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:21.680
What?

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:25.060
Not that I know how much
I was able to contribute to this body...

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.390
but somehow, I managed
to see this job through to the end!

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:33.360
Oh, would you like some tea?
Please feel free to take a break here.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.400
Oh, please don't go to any trouble.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:39.950
I'm truly grateful
to all you Red Blood Cells.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:43.280
Running all over this body
is quite commendable.

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:44.740
Oh no.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:48.500
Uh, Sebaceous Gland Cell,
what kind of work did you do?

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.210
It wasn't much of a job.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:57.670
All I ever did was store sebum here
to protect the body and preserve moisture.

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.590
Oh really?
But that's such an important job!

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:06.390
No, all I did was hole up in this room
and wait for the sebum to build up.

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:11.150
But now at last,
I've stored a sufficient amount.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:13.860
And I can do something useful
for this body.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:16.820
How are you going to
transport all this sebum?

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:22.200
I'm going to rupture myself along with
this bag and scatter it outside this body.

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:23.160
- What?
- What?

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:26.290
<i>When a Sebaceous Gland dies,</i>

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:29.910
<i>the expanded fat stored within it
bursts simultaneously,</i>

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:32.630
<i>and it leaks out of the pores,
all over the skin.</i>

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:36.300
But if you do that, then you'll...

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.840
Forgive me. It seems like my time is up.

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:44.090
As it wouldn't do to expose you
to such a filthy sight, if you please...

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:45.430
Oh, right.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:46.430
Let's go.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:53.440
Now then, as this is my grand exit...

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:57.360
I just hope this won't generate any ROS.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.620
<i>Sebaceous Gland Cell...</i>

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:09.870
That's ROS!

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.960
It's the one I delivered!

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.000
What's this smell?
My eyes are stinging!

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:15.880
It stinks!

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.840
Nonenal detected in a scalp pore!

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.880
It's producing an acrid odor!

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:23.430
An acrid odor from a scalp pore?

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:25.890
Body odor from aging?

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:28.010
<i>Body odor from aging.</i>

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:35.650
<i>When the palmitoleic acid contained in the fat
secreted by the Sebaceous Glands is oxidized by ROS,</i>

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:39.860
<i>it's converted into a substance called "nonenal,"
generating body odor.</i>

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:41.820
What the cell is this smell?

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:43.280
My eyes!

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:47.240
- It's my fault!
- Huh?

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:51.200
Sebaceous Gland Cell put his life
on the line to do this job...

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:55.250
but because the oxygen I delivered
turned into ROS again—

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.750
It's not your fault! There's another reason
why there's more ROS.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:02.970
Has this ever happened to you?
Has any oxygen you delivered turned into ROS?

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:06.890
Well, maybe not that,
but that's only by chance, and—

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:07.890
No.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:10.810
- It's just the way it is.
- Huh?

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:13.520
You and I are different!

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:15.600
Hold on!

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:16.770
Stay away from me!

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:21.360
A role model like you
shouldn't be hanging out with me.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.000
Hey, you look pretty wiped.

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:40.590
Don't avoid us like that.

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:45.050
We're all Red Blood Cells.
All we want is to have each others' backs.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.010
Let's go get a boost together.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.980
Where are we?

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:57.100
The small intestine.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:59.730
You can feel the effects to some extent
no matter where you are,

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:01.650
but these are the VIP seats.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:06.200
Only a handful of Red Blood Cells ever get
any praise no matter how hard we work.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:09.450
The fatigue just keeps building up,
but who's worried about us?

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:12.540
So, that's the thing that brings us salvation.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:13.620
That?

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:17.160
It won't be long now, I bet.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.460
The ingested nutrients
are arriving in the small intestine!

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:23.920
Not again!

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:27.760
Is this alcohol?

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.340
No. This is...

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.430
Manna from heaven!

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:42.110
Here it comes! I can feel it surging!

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:45.280
- Wh-What's this?
- What do you say?

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.240
Can't you feel that power surge?

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:50.910
It rains down at least five times a day,

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:54.290
and it totally puts that straight arrow
classmate of yours to shame!

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:57.250
Whoa!

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:58.460
Blood vessel, dilating!

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:00.120
The blood flow is about to increase!

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:04.800
All right, let's deliver like crazy!

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:05.750
Yeah!

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:07.760
<i>Energy drinks.</i>

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:13.100
<i>The general term for beverages
sold as pick-me-ups or as dietary supplements</i>

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:14.640
<i>to counter physical fatigue.</i>

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:18.520
<i>They contain caffeine
which enhances mental alertness,</i>

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:22.610
<i>and arginine, known to boost energy
and expand the blood vessels.</i>

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:24.770
<i>Known to be effective in physical recovery.</i>

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:28.490
Hey, hold up!

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:32.030
What, is that you? Long time no see!
Are you doing okay?

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:35.280
Yeah. Looks like you're on a roll there, huh?

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:39.250
Thanks to all the caffeine and arginine!
We've been getting a lot of it lately!

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:44.920
True. Thanks to that stuff, I'm not so tired,
and I've been working more efficiently,

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:49.050
but once the effects wear off,
I start feeling a little listless, and—

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:52.510
When that happens, all you have to do
is get showered with it again.

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:55.300
See, here it comes! Whoo!

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:58.560
The second it washes over me,
it gives me instant energy!

00:15:58.560 --> 00:15:59.930
Do you think it's okay?

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:03.100
I mean, it's not great to feel exhausted
after working, but...

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:05.360
What are you saying?

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:08.280
I was just wondering
if it's too good to be true or not.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:09.690
There must be some kind of catch—

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:13.240
There you go again! Mouthing off
like the role model that you are!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.950
Remember what they told us?
That as long as we're Red Blood Cells,

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:18.830
all that matters
is how much oxygen we can deliver.

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:23.040
No matter how we go about it,
as long as we produce, it's all good!

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:27.000
See? It's surging now! See ya!

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:37.560
Which way?

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:40.890
Go, go, go!

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:47.110
Jeez, you're still here?

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:51.990
You sure took your time on that delivery.
What happened to you, Top Rookie?

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:55.240
Well, the vein's all tangled up in here—

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:57.990
Wh-What's that?

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.200
What's going on?

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.330
The capillaries in the nasal cavity
have ruptured!

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.420
It appears to have caused hemorrhaging
from the Kiesselbach's plexus!

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:09.420
<i>Too much arginine in the system can lead
to excessive dilation of the blood vessels,</i>

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:11.380
<i>making one more susceptible
to nosebleeds.</i>

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:12.840
Nosebleed!

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:18.890
Whoa!

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:29.820
Hey, over here!

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:31.030
Reach out your hand!

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:32.940
All right!

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:35.150
Are you okay?

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:38.070
No problem! I don't need your help!

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.870
C'mon, what are you doing? Hurry!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:46.210
Come on!

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.170
This way! Hurry!

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:50.880
No good!

00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:53.050
I have no strength!

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.010
Huh? Why not?

00:17:56.050 --> 00:18:00.970
I feel listless. The effects...
The effects have worn off.

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:03.890
<i>Caffeine addiction.</i>

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:08.770
<i>Caused by the neurotoxic nature
of caffeine itself.</i>

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:14.070
<i>Cessation of caffeine often triggers headaches,
lethargy and other withdrawal symptoms.</i>

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:19.070
That kid got over exposed
to caffeine and arginine!

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.080
Please!

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:26.620
Give me some caffeine!
Some arginine! Somebody! Hurry!

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:29.290
This is no time to be talking like that!

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.550
Give it up! He can't be saved!

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:35.420
But no...

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:40.430
It turned out just like you said.

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:44.270
It's because I got too dependent
on that stuff.

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:48.730
Losers are losers no matter what they do.

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:54.940
I was always the first to bolt,
and all I did was get in your way!

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:56.740
A guy like me...

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.490
doesn't deserve to live.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:02.120
Don't give up! There isn't a single cell
who doesn't deserve to live!

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:05.620
At the very least, I...

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:08.330
It was because of you!

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:11.830
I decided to give it my all to keep up with you
because you were there!

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:16.510
And there were so many times that I was able
to stay put and make a stand because I had you!

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:21.180
There's only so much
that a Red Blood Cell can do on his own.

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:23.350
That's why...

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:24.810
I need you!

00:19:26.270 --> 00:19:28.730
I need you, my precious friend!

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:36.230
Don't give me that!

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:41.700
Jeez, listen to you,
always saying the right thing!

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:43.950
Because of you...

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:45.950
Because of you...

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:52.120
I want to live just a little longer now, dammit!

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:58.710
One more push!

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:12.900
Damn you!

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:25.990
Look at you, totally out of breath!

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:30.540
What happened to you, Top Rookie?

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.170
You're going there again?

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:47.970
Enough with the teen drama!

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:51.180
PLATELETS

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:51.180
You're in the way! Get lost already!

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:52.980
Right! Sorry about that!

00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:58.610
Take good care of your friend.

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:10.120
Yo, you're in the zone again today, huh?

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:13.500
But it must be about to wear off.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:16.080
Come on, let's go to our usual spot.

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:25.050
Sorry. I'm going to pass.

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:28.010
All right, I've got a delivery to make.

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:30.260
Don't you need it
because you have a delivery to make?

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:36.270
What I need right now
isn't caffeine or arginine.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:37.480
What do you need, then?

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:39.150
That...

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:41.570
I'm too embarrassed to tell you.

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:21.540
PREVIEW

00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:23.590
This body hasn't gotten any sleep
for two full days.

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:24.750
CALVES

00:23:24.380 --> 00:23:26.760
The pulmonary embolism
formed in the deep vein

00:23:26.260 --> 00:23:27.420
PULMONARY EMBOLISM

00:23:26.760 --> 00:23:28.300
is now advancing
toward the upper torso!

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:30.090
QUICK THINKING

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:32.760
What can we do
to overcome this crisis?

00:23:31.140 --> 00:23:34.050
CALVES, PULMONARY EMBOLISM,
AND QUICK THINKING
